386→                        <div id="content">Call $n$ <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weird_number" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer ugc" target="_blank">weird</a> if $\sigma(n)\geq 2n$ and $n$ is not pseudoperfect, that is, it is not the sum of any set of its divisors.<br><br>Are there any odd weird numbers? Are there infinitely many primitive weird numbers, i.e. those such that no proper divisor of $n$ is weird?</div>
387→                        <div id="problem_id"><a href="/470">#470</a>: <a href="#cite-BeEr74-470" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('BeEr74','470'); return false;">[BeEr74]</a><a href="#cite-Er77c-470" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er77c','470'); return false;">[Er77c,p.47]</a><a href="#cite-ErGr80-470" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('ErGr80','470'); return false;">[ErGr80,p.94]</a></div>
